<PageLayout
  title="Our Story — Leslie 'Hope' Houston | Silver Lining of Hope"
  description="Silver Lining of Hope was founded by Megan Tomlinson in honor of her mother, Leslie 'Hope' Houston. This is the story behind our mission."
  heading="Our story"
  intro="Every organization has a mission statement. Ours has a name: Hope."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'About', href: '/about' },
    { label: 'Our story', href: '/about/our-story' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="container--narrow section prose">
    <figure class="memorial-frame story-photo">
      <img
        src="/images/leslie-hope-houston.jpg"
        alt="Leslie 'Hope' Houston smiling outdoors"
        width="480"
        height="600"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption>Leslie "Hope" Houston</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>
      In October 2024, Leslie "Hope" Houston — a mother, a friend, a woman
      whose middle name would come to carry a movement — was killed. In the
      weeks that followed, her family faced what too many families face: a
      case that wasn't moving, questions that weren't being answered, and a
      system that seemed to expect them to simply wait.
    </p>
    <p>
      Her daughter, Megan Tomlinson, refused to wait. For seven months she did
      the work herself — requesting records, building timelines, organizing
      evidence, and pressing for the case to get the attention it deserved.
      That independent research helped get her mother's case reopened, and
      charges were filed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Somewhere in those seven months, a hard truth became impossible to
      ignore: most families don't know how to do what Megan did. They don't
      know what records they're entitled to, how to preserve what they find,
      or how to be heard without being dismissed. And the investigators
      working these cases are often stretched across far more cases than any
      person could give full attention to.
    </p>
    <p>
      Silver Lining of Hope, Inc was founded to close that gap — to give
      every family the investigative research, organization, and steady
      advocacy that Leslie's family had to build from nothing, and to give
      law enforcement a prepared, professional partner instead of a cold
      file.
    </p>

    <h2>What "Silver Lining" means to us</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing good erases a loss like this. But out of the darkest thing that
      ever happened to our founder's family came a thin line of light — proof
      that persistence works, that cases can move, and that one prepared
      person can change an outcome. We exist to be that line of light for
      other families. That is the silver lining, and it is drawn in Hope's
      name.
    </p>

    <h2>Where we're going</h2>
    <p>
      Our work is organized into the four pillars of HOPE — Homicides,
      Outreach &amp; advocacy, Persons missing, and Education &amp; reform —
      and anchored by The Missing Link, our project to build a complete,
      public, searchable directory of Indiana's missing, expanding across the
      Midwest.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/programs">Explore our programs</a> ·
      <a href="/get-help">Get help with a case</a> ·
      <a href="/donate">Support the mission</a>
    </p>
  </div>

